<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prolaya Vema Reddi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1325–1353</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prolaya Vema Reddi was the founder of the Reddi kingdom in coastal Andhra. A former follower of the Kakatiyas, he joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musunuri-nayakas">Musunuri Nayaks</a> in the revolt against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a> and around 1325 established his own rule, with his capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/addanki">Addanki</a>. He restored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> temples and grants, and his successors moved the capital to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kondavidu">Kondavidu</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prolaya-vema-reddi.jpg" alt="Prolaya Vema Reddi" width="320" height="356" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pedhireddi · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reddi_KIngdom_at_its_peakl.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
